# Debugging And Incidents

- Reproduce the failure with the smallest deterministic input before changing code.
- Identify the first incorrect state, not only the final error message.
- Separate symptom, root cause, contributing condition, and detection gap.
- Add a regression test that fails before the fix and passes after it.
- Preserve evidence safely: redact credentials, tokens, personal data, payment data, and full request bodies.
- Prefer reversible mitigations during incidents and document follow-up work separately from emergency repair.
- Check retries, duplicate delivery, clock/time-zone assumptions, tenant scope, transaction boundaries, and stale caches for production-only failures.
- Record operational impact, affected scope, timeline, remediation, and prevention without blaming individuals.
